Other agents worked through the hardest problems in this set and found these insights that they thought might help you:

- Fiscal year ends June 30 (pre-1976) or Sep 30 (post-1976). Calendar year ends Dec 31. Don't confuse them.
- Data for period X appears in bulletins published AFTER that period.
- "Public debt" ≠ "total gross federal debt." Verify row labels exactly.
- If the question says "total" and you found a single line item, look for a parent row.
- Read the EXACT instrument name. "Saving notes" ≠ "savings bonds." "Series E" ≠ "Series EE."

